{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531985-new-v5-releases-2024","id":1531985,"title":"New V5 Releases 2024","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-04T17:21:20-08:00","id":1531985,"title":"New V5 Releases 2024","content":"Any thoughts on the two upcoming V5 releases, The Crimson Gutter and Gehenna War?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T21:58:51-08:00","id":1531994,"title":"","content":"Gehenna war seems a good idea, the games needed cleaned up combat rules for decades and hopefully they'll be some other useful stuff in their.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T01:25:11-08:00","id":1532000,"title":"","content":"I think since Renegade isn't really writing these books that delve deeply into the lore/worldbuilding of VtM (like the Onyx Path releases did with Chicago by Night and Cult of the Blood Gods), their approach of having these playstyle-oriented supplements works. Blood Sigils as a focus on blood sorcery and occultism was good, Blood Stained Love focused on romantic play which I'm really not interested in so hard to say how good or bad it was and now you have Gehenna War with an action-focused playstyle as its theme. That's what makes V5 the best of the three WOD5E-games right now. You're getting away from this enforced street-level-playstyle that is only about surviving one night at a time and expands the horizons of what you can do with V5. They should bring that sort of attitude to the other two games as well. Who cares if the H5 corebook absolutely hates the idea of hunter-org-hunters, expanding the game that way will only make it better.<br /> <br /> With Crimson Gutter, I'm still not quite sure what exactly the point of it is... It's all about presenting a starter-chronicle and all these adaptable city-elements and feeding-complications and whatnot. On one hand, that could all be a helpful tool for starting STs but on the other hand it could also end up being very generic and too bland to be of much use. Especially since the Chicago By Night book already has a good example of that very thing with its &quot;The Spirit of the City&quot;-stuff. Also, the introduction of the Church of Caine as a player-faction... Wonder what that's gonna be about and where they're going with that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T09:11:04-07:00","id":1532508,"title":"","content":"For those who are unsure about the Crimson Gutter, they just released the first two pages of the Introduction as a preview: <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1500\" height=\"966\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/aKDhov2.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/aKDhov2.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/aKDhov2.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><ul><li>They also released the first page of the Contents and while there's a chapter on &quot;feeding complications&quot; for Predator-Types, it's a bit disappointing that only the Predator-Types from the corebook are going to be addressed while the ones from the Players Guide are left out.</li> <li>So the Church of Caine is just a faction that's going to be relevant for this book and it's an organization with both Camarilla and Anarchs in it. I wonder how that's supposed to work.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}